From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:40:20 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] A template's chunk packets are kept in a mapped frame file
 beside its store

The compressed full-chunk packets of a template were made on the heap, 8 to 11 MB a
map, for every server on the box and again for every match once the last world on
the map had gone (3% of a server's allocation). Frames made for chunks still as the
template has them are now written, a few dozen at a time, to
athena-frames-<fingerprint>-p<id>-l<level>-t<threshold>.bin, renamed into place and
mapped read only; a chunk with the same sections and biomes is sent from the
mapping. -Dathena.disableFrameFiles=true keeps them on the heap.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

